; BOUNCE BONANZA - song 9, course 2 "Little Hop": "Little Hop" (SPEC.md 130.20)
;
; A major at 149 BPM with a HARD skip: a 16th is a row, and the rows
; alternate seven and four sub-ticks (`groove 7 4`), so an 8th is always 11
; and every pair of 16ths is long-short - a skipping rope, a ball hopping.
; A pattern is two bars of 4/4, 3.2 s.
;
; The second tutorial course teaches the HOP and rubber's "and again" (the
; double jump), so the tune is made of them: its MOTIF is two hops, the
; second higher - a skip up a fourth, a breath, the same skip up a sixth -
; then a bounce down the chord:
;   e16 a16 r8 e16 >c+16 r8 <b8 a8 f+8 a8        (over A)
; Plain, sure harmony for a newcomer: A D | A F#m Bm E7 (a half close) |
; A D | D E A (the full close). The bridge goes legato on the RECORDER over
; a string pad and a half-time hop in the bass, F#m D | Bm E | D C#m | Bm7
; E7, and the BREAK is the lesson itself: hop, and again, four times
; climbing over E, the chiparp's sparkle on the landing, and back to A.
;
; The intro is the ball hopping onto the course over E: hop, and again (an
; octave), a breath, then a bouncing run down the E7 scale onto the motif.
; The AdLib keeps its intro bare (the lesson of First Roll's, whose horn and
; stabs buried the taps): bar 1 is the music box's hops over the bass, the
; kick and the hats alone - no chord at all - and bar 2 has one soft harp E7
; an octave BELOW the run. Rendered, every intro note is the loudest pitch
; in its 16th on the AdLib, as on the speaker.
;
; Intro, A A' B C A'' for ever: the loop is 11 patterns, 35.4 s.
;
; Style borrowed, not notes: Fairway's harp "pah" on 2 and 4, Bounce Trial's
; octave-popping pluck bass and its `q`-gap spelling, First Roll's bare
; intro. The lead is the MUSIC BOX (a toy's bell, struck, so every hop
; speaks at once on the AdLib - the lute was tried and rendered at half the
; bass's level), the recorder takes the bridge a notch softer (v12).
;
; A note followed by a written rest is spelled as ONE note with a `q` gap,
; as Bounce Trial does: a hop `e16 a16 r8` is `e16 q12 a8. q1` (the 8th's
; eleven sub-ticks gated off), the same sound on both arms, two bytes fewer.
;
; THE SPEAKER: the lead carries it, and every hop's 8th rest is where
; `spkbass` lets the bass through: under a hop the bass BOUNCES in octaves
; (root, octave, root, octave), so each rest is an octave pop under the ball.
; The break's first bar drops the bass on purpose - hops in the air, the kick
; alone. Kick, snare and clap blip; the skipping hats are the AdLib's. Every
; phrase names its instrument and volume at its start.

song littlehop "Little Hop"
groove 7 4
unit 16
rows 32
measure 16
spkbass
voice lead musicbox
voice bass pluckbass
voice chord harp

; --- the intro: hop, and again, over E -------------------------------------------
lead LI = @musicbox v13 o4 e16 q12 b8. q1 e16 q12 >e8. q1 r4 <b16 >d16 e16 g+16 |
          b8 a8 g+8 f+8 e8 d8 c+8 <b8 |
bass BI = o2 q12 e4. q1 >e8 q12 <e4. q1 >e8 | q12 <e4 q1 >e8 <e8 q12 g+4 q1 b8 >d8 |
chord CI = @harp v8 o3 r1 | [d e g+]2 r2 |
drum DI = k4 h8 h8 k4 h8 h8 | k8 h16 h16 s8 h16 h16 k8 s16 s16 T16 T16 t8 |

; --- A: hop, and again --------------------------------------------------------------
lead LA1 = @musicbox v13 o4 e16 q12 a8. q1 e16 q12 >c+8. q1 <b8 a8 f+8 a8 |
           f+16 q12 a8. q1 f+16 q12 >d8. q1 c+8 <a8 b4 |
lead LA2 = @musicbox v13 o4 e16 q12 a8. q1 e16 q12 >e8. q1 d8 c+8 <a8 >c+8 |
           <b8 >d8 f+8 d8 e8 r8 <b8 g+8 |
lead LA3 = @musicbox v13 o4 f+16 q12 a8. q1 f+16 q12 >d8. q1 <e16 q12 g+8. q1 e16 q12 >e8. q1 |
           c+8 <a8 >e8 c+8 @chiparp a4 r4 |
bass BA1 = o2 a8 >a8 <a8 >a8 q12 <e4 q1 >e8 <e8 | d8 >d8 <d8 >d8 q12 <a4 q1 >a8 <a8 |
bass BA2 = o2 a8 >a8 <a8 >a8 q12 <f+4 q1 >f+8 <f+8 | q12 b4 q1 >b8 <b8 e8 >e8 <e8 >e8 |
bass BA3 = o2 d8 >d8 <d8 >d8 <e8 >e8 <e8 >e8 | q12 <a4 q1 >a8 <a8 e8 >e8 <a8 >a8 |
chord CA1 = @harp v9 o4 r4 [c+ e a]4 r4 [c+ e a]4 | r4 [d f+ a]4 r4 [d f+ a]4 |
chord CA2 = @harp v9 o4 r4 [c+ e a]4 r4 [c+ f+ a]4 | r4 [d f+ b]4 r4 [d e g+]4 |
chord CA3 = @harp v9 o4 r4 [d f+ a]4 r4 [e g+ b]4 | r4 [c+ e a]4 r4 [c+ e a]4 |
drum DA = k8 h16 h16 s8 h16 h16 k8 h16 h16 s8 h16 h16 | k8 h16 h16 s8 h16 h16 k8 h16 h16 s8 h16 h16 |
drum DF = k8 h16 h16 s8 h16 h16 k8 h16 h16 s8 h16 h16 | k8 h16 h16 s8 h16 h16 k8 s16 s16 T16 T16 t8 |

; --- B: the bridge, legato on the recorder over a string pad ------------------------
lead LB1 = @recorder v12 o5 c+4. <a8 f+8 a8 >c+8 e8 | d4. <a8 f+8 a8 >d8 f+8 |
lead LB2 = @recorder v12 o5 f+4. e8 d4 <b4 | >e4. <b8 g+8 b8 >e8 r8 |
lead LB3 = @recorder v12 o5 f+4. d8 <a8 >d8 f+8 a8 | g+4. e8 c+8 e8 g+8 r8 |
lead LB4 = @recorder v12 o5 f+4 d4 <b4 a4 | g+8 b8 >d8 e8 @chiparp e4 r4 |
bass BB1 = o2 q12 f+4. q1 >f+8 q12 <c+4. q1 >c+8 | q12 <d4. q1 >d8 q12 <a4. q1 >a8 |
bass BB2 = o2 q12 b4. q1 >b8 q12 <f+4. q1 >f+8 | q12 <e4. q1 >e8 q12 <b4. q1 >b8 |
bass BB3 = o2 q12 d4. q1 >d8 q12 <a4. q1 >a8 | q12 <c+4. q1 >c+8 q12 <g+4. q1 >g+8 |
bass BB4 = o2 q12 b4. q1 >b8 q12 <f+4. q1 >f+8 | q12 <e4. q1 >e8 <g+8 b8 >d8 e8 |
chord CB1 = @strings v9 o4 [c+ f+ a]1 | [d f+ a]1 |
chord CB2 = @strings v9 o4 [d f+ b]1 | [e g+ b]1 |
chord CB3 = @strings v9 o4 [d f+ a]1 | [c+ e g+]1 |
chord CB4 = @strings v9 o4 [d f+ a]1 | [d e g+]1 |
drum DB = k4 h16 h16 h8 c4 h16 h16 k8 | k4 h16 h16 h8 c4 h16 h16 h8 |

; --- C: the break - hop, and again, climbing over E -----------------------------------
lead LC = @musicbox v13 o4 e16 q12 b8. q1 e16 q12 >e8. q1 <g+16 q12 >d8. q1 <g+16 q12 >g+8. q1 |
          <b16 q12 >e8. q1 <b16 q12 >b8. q1 @chiparp e4 r4 |
bass BC = o2 q67 e1 | q1 r2 q12 e4 q1 >e8 <b8 |
drum DC = k8 h16 h16 r8 h16 h16 k8 h16 h16 r8 h16 h16 | s16 s16 s16 s16 s16 s16 s16 s16 s8 s8 T8 t8 |

order LI  BI  CI  DI          ; 0: the intro, E
order LA1 BA1 CA1 DA          ; 1: A   A D - the loop comes back here
order LA2 BA2 CA2 DF          ; 2:     A F#m Bm E7, the half close
order LA1 BA1 CA1 DA          ; 3: A'  A D
order LA3 BA3 CA3 DF          ; 4:     D E A, the full close
order LB1 BB1 CB1 DB          ; 5: B   F#m D
order LB2 BB2 CB2 DB          ; 6:     Bm E
order LB3 BB3 CB3 DB          ; 7:     D C#m
order LB4 BB4 CB4 DF          ; 8:     Bm7 E7, the spring
order LC  BC  -   DC          ; 9: C   the break: hop, and again
order LA1 BA1 CA1 DA          ; 10: A'' A D
order LA3 BA3 CA3 DF          ; 11:     D E A
loop 1
